WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.399 --> 00:00:01.429 align:start position:0%
 
that  is  empirical proof  that migration is still happening  between this coast and britain we've  watched these people about 40 of them  carrying a very large inflatable boat  putting it in the water crowding onto it  they're now trying to get the engine  working and they've done all that in  full site of the french police a unit of  whom have been stationed on the beach  and have been watching a police  helicopter came overhead and was  watching what happened and they can't  say they hadn't been born because about  half an hour before this  another boat set off same thing same  sort of boat also with about 40 people  on it and it left these shores heading  over towards the british coast and on  that occasion too the french police  watched and did nothing we asked them  why that was the case  now nobody told us officially but i  spoke to one of the officers who said  that there were only eight of them  confronted by what was about 40 people  on the boat and another 40 people around  them the message being quite clearly  that they thought they were outnumbered  the other thing i think to take from  this is that sometimes you can get the  impression that people smuggling between  europe and the british coast is all very  very subterfuge it's done at night it's  done in the small hours and very often  it is but look around us  this is broad daylight these people  carried their boat along a beach in full  view not just of the police but of dog  walkers have passed us by and of us  this  is what people trafficking  looks like sometimes not always that  slick undercover operation  sometimes  as brazen as that

